WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.370
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.330
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.180
Kanuka Appears

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:14.190
Police Academy:
Okutama Branch

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.230
One, two, three, four!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.650
Shinshi, you're slow!

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.490
Yes, Sir!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.070
One, two, three, four!

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.450
Good, your movements
are getting smoother!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.700
One, two, three, four!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.620
Asuma, pass the soy sauce?

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:05.580
Sure.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.580
Thank you.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.450
You're in a good mood.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.870
It's been a long,
hard battle.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.750
They've totally
controlled us.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.300
We haven't had a moment
of rest or relaxation.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.430
Nothing but Labor
training and lectures.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.850
We've had a dismal two weeks...
it's enough to make me throw up!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.230
And now,
it's finally over!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.770
We've done well.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.520
There's still the
announcement this afternoon.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.070
That'll be a picnic,
compared to all this training.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.200
Is there really going to be a
competition fight, beforehand?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.610
Are you okay, Shinshi?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.160
I have a weak stomach.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.790
Well if you can't eat that,
I'll take it!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.670
Bring on your Labors!
No one can beat me!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.800
Don't believe me?
I'll prove it!

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.550
No, no!
Look over there!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.010
Who's that?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.430
She's getting onboard.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.620
She's pretty good.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.290
Is it safe to maneuver
a Labor like that?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:38.290
Theoretically, the Ingram can
match any human movement, but...

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.210
But?

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.050
Such a massive machine
produces incredible stress.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.850
Now, for the main event
of today's announcement:

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.770
A Labor combat
tournament!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:03.490
This will decide the composition
of our teams, so do your best.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.200
Any questions?

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.820
Yes! Yes!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.120
All in good time.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.910
Captain!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.870
Don't worry.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.170
I'm Lieutenant Clancy Kanuka,
of the New York City Police.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:26.180
I've come to Japan for advanced
training. Pleased to meet you.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.850
New York?

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.890
All rise!

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.310
Why?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.060
Pay your respects to
a police lieutenant!

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.770
Ota, don't be so formal.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.230
But...

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.950
You junior officers
wouldn't understand!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.040
There are ranks and classes
in the police department.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:01.420
Respect your superiors, or
you'll never get promoted.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:05.840
But what's her name, Kanuka,
is from the New York police.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.430
That doesn't matter!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.050
Yeah, the lower classes
believe that junk.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.270
Why, you!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.730
So you have to win the
tournament to pilot the Ingram?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.940
You could look
at it that way.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.190
What pressure!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.860
We need to
choose wisely.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:37.250
The Ingram records and adapts
to its pilot's motion patterns.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.960
So it will only
accept one person?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.840
Exactly. Once we choose
a pilot, it's hard to change.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.010
So this tournament
makes sense.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:52.050
I see! But I wanna
be the pilot!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.510
Don't whine.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.560
Okay! But I have an idea!

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.740
That ought to do it!

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.460
Shige, inspect the Ingrams.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.340
Yes, Sir.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.960
What the heck?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.260
What's wrong?

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:37.140
"This is mine."

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.560
Erase that.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:43.850
This is mine?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.820
That was quick.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.780
How does it look?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.450
We have an
excellent teacher.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.070
Good work.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:01.710
I enjoyed myself.
But they're a strange group.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.080
Will they do?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.960
Well, they're certainly
different from Division 1.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:15.550
They're talented, or just a bunch
of losers... I'm not sure.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.810
Make up your mind.
Are you praising them, or not?

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.850
I thought I was praising them.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:27.110
I can judge their skill later.
After all, that's why I came.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.820
Did you bring the uniform?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.570
Yes. Are you sure
she won't be offended?

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.320
She's the one
who asked for it.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.470
Why is she wearing a
Second Section uniform?

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.600
How should I know?
Hey, look over there!

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:09.230
It's Gomioka from Division 1.
He even brought his Labor.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.440
Could it be?

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.230
It could.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.780
- What could?
- Look...

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.370
I love you, Miki!
Good luck!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.870
Who's Miki?

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.710
My full name is Mikiyasu.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.710
That's your wife?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:29.840
Yes.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.300
You're lucky.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.130
You weaklings!

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:41.640
Now, to conclude your training
on the Model 98-AV Ingram...

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.970
we will stage a
combat tournament.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.270
And to provide a
worthwhile challenge...

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.610
we have Lieutenant Gomioka
of Division 1 in his Model 97.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.530
I knew it.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.870
Also participating...

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.950
is Lieutenant Clancy Kanuka,
of the New York City Police.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.120
I'm pleased to announce...

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.750
she'll be joining Division 2 for
6 months of advanced training.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.380
Looks like we have
some tough competition.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.550
Here are the match orders.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.680
Rounds 1 and 2 will
use the training Labors.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.220
The final round
will use the Ingram.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.810
Match 1 is in ten minutes:
Shinohara vs. Izumi.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.350
That was quick.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:30.770
Asuma...

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.820
I...

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.280
I won't lose!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.700
Ingram Machine 2

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.710
Bull Dog

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.430
Bow!

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:01.890
Begin!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.720
Let's go!

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.440
Impudent child!
Surrender!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.860
I'm not a child!
I'm a young lady!

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:22.030
They don't look
very tense.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.700
The energy of youth. They're
like well-oiled machines.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.090
I win!

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.350
That's enough,
Officer Izumi!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.430
What was that
supposed to be?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.850
Do you suspect
some deception?

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.100
That was deliberate.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:12:00.690
That Labor must be defective!
Its leg just gave out on me!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:05.120
This is serious! If there's
a maintenance problem...

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:10.870
Oh, no! If anything,
it was a factory flaw.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:13.500
But it was built
by your company!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.210
My father's company!
I had nothing to do with it!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:23.590
Asuma Shinohara... Shinohara
Heavy Industries. Shinohara!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.930
Asuma, you're a second-
generation Shinohara!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:34.310
Why become a civil servant,
if you own a Labor factory?

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.110
My dad swindled me.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:42.320
Good luck, Miki!
Don't get hurt, sweetie!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:47.030
This will all be over
in five seconds!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.490
I hate this.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.450
Bow!

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:58.130
Had enough?

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.550
Penalty!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.420
Mr. Sakuma,
criminals don't bow!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.340
In a real fight, the first
move guarantees victory!

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.010
You cheated!
You coward!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.810
Winning is all
that matters!

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.230
So you think this is funny?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.400
Does Shinshi look
kind of strange?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:27.530
What's so funny?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.330
Stop! Both sides
must bow, first!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.170
What's so funny?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.630
Stop it!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.590
Funny now?
Funny now?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.550
Are you trying
to kill me?

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.760
Officer Shinshi,
you're disqualified!

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.230
Shinshi is surprisingly
dangerous.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.520
I'll have to file that
for future reference.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.930
He's such a nice guy, but...

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.390
Officer Yamazaki
forfeits.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:41.440
Round 2: Officer Noa Izumi
vs. Officer Isao Ota.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.240
Bow!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.410
I won't fall
for that trick!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.800
My gun!

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.350
That's enough,
Officer Izumi.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.230
The neck joint
seems a bit fragile.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:26.530
Perhaps it's just vulnerable
to a blow from above.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.110
I don't think it's the machine
that's your problem here.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.530
Your tactics are vulgar.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.500
Well, let's see what
kind of fight she prefers.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.720
So what's Gomioka like?

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:53.800
Fourth rank in judo, third in
kendo, second rank in aikido.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.970
Composed and calm... the
perfect portrait of an officer.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.560
If she's as good, it should
be an interesting match.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.520
So it must be pretty important
to have hand-to-hand skills.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.320
I think you're
better off without them.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.490
A Labor is power!
Power decides everything!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.820
What if your opponent
can match your power?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:16.830
I'm filled with a
fighting spirit!

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:17.780
Big deal.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.330
Lieutenant Kanuka wins.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.670
What happened?
What happened?

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:33.720
A shoulder throw! She executed
a perfect shoulder throw!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:39.350
In the final match, Officer Izumi
will face Lieutenant Kanuka.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:42.390
This should be interesting.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:46.360
Kanuka's too good
for Division 2.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:47.610
Do you want her?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.190
Would you like her to
transfer to Division 1?

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.030
You'd never let her go.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.110
How true.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.570
I don't think I can win.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.740
Wisdom and bravery.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.790
In a real fight, you can't
choose your enemy.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:06.380
You can't run away.
You have to do your duty.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:07.880
And so...

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:08.920
What?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.420
Wisdom and bravery will
see you through, somehow.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.260
I don't really
understand, but okay.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:24.810
Now, the final battle: Officer
Izumi vs. Lieutenant Kanuka.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:26.520
Bow!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:32.820
Begin!

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.870
Get back! You'll lose
if you lock arms!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.840
Wisdom and bravery.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.600
Electromagnetic
police baton.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.260
Too late!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.240
Come on!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.700
Why, you!

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.620
If you lose your head,
you've lost!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.670
What's she doing?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.590
She's staying
out of arm's reach.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:42.680
Well, that way she can't lose.
But she can't win, either.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:07.910
Noa was defiant, but that
left them in a stalemate.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:17.590
Kanuka contained Noa
with minimal wasted motion.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.680
"Coward! Unfair! Why
don't you do something!"

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.510
Ota ridiculed Noa, but
she stood her ground.

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:35.230
No one had expected such
a long, drawn-out match.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:45.330
You'd better finish the fight
before your power runs out!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:49.290
But which is wisdom
and which is bravery?

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.540
It's good that you
held out so long...

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.790
but you don't have to
match her skill. Just attack!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.800
My batteries!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.270
She's coming for me!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.250
That's enough!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.420
I did it!

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.630
Lieutenant Clancy
Kanuka wins!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.510
What? Why?

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.050
Because of this.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.770
Stop!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.950
You wasted too much
motion, Officer Izumi.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:11.200
If you'd used more precision,
you'd still have power left.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:31.470
Quiet, please. Now, the
moment you've been waiting for:

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.020
Number one Forward,
Ingram Pilot:

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.310
Officer Noa Izumi.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.980
Really? You're serious?

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.110
What would you do
if I were lying?

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.150
I did it!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:49.200
Number one Backup, command
car: Officer Asuma Shinohara.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.700
Yes, Sir.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.120
Number one Labor carrier:
Officer Hiromi Yamazaki.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.160
Yes, Sir.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.380
Number two Forward,
Ingram pilot: Officer Isao Ota.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:04.420
Backup, command car:
Lieutenant Clancy Kanuka.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:09.300
Labor carrier: Officer
Mikiyasu Shinshi. That is all.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:14.770
Ota, do you know why
I chose you as the forward?

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:20.480
Yes, Sir! I can't give orders
to Lieutenant Kanuka!

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:24.530
No! It's because I'll only
be here for six months.

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:29.280
You shouldn't adapt the Ingram
to someone who's going to leave.

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:32.450
Six months...

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:36.580
It's going to be an
interesting half year.

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:16.100
This is Special Vehicles, Section 2.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.520
We're stuck out here in the
middle of nowhere.

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:21.520
Life in this department has been
really weird these days...

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:23.850
I guess I just have to get used to it.

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:25.810
Stupid! You don't have the
time for that!

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:28.110
Ingram #3 just sank to
the bottom of the sea!

00:24:28.150 --> 00:24:29.110
You better go get it.

